 ## Background
-The concept of rendering specific materials within volumes dates back to early volume visualization work [S2, unofficial]. Drebin, Carpenter, and Hanrahan developed techniques for rendering volumes containing mixtures of materials, such as CT data containing bone, muscle, and flesh, by creating material percentage volumes [S2, unofficial]. Modern implementations extend this to procedural generation for clouds [3480-procedural-volumetric-cloud-rendering.md] and neural representations like DVGO [12839-dvgo-density-and-color-rendering.md]. Specific rendering modes like DRRs and MIPs are implemented in GPU volume renderers [S1, unofficial], while heat haze and volumetric geometry modes are specialized features in production renderers like V-Ray for 3ds Max [S3].
